# shadcn/ui — the ONLY UI source

**ONLY shadcn/ui components may be used for the UI in this project. ABSOLUTELY NO custom UI may be created.**

This is a hard rule with no exceptions. Every visible element (buttons, inputs, forms, cards, dialogs, menus, tables, badges, alerts, tabs, etc.) must be a shadcn/ui component imported from `@/components/ui`.

## Absolute prohibitions

- **NO custom UI components.** Do not create bespoke buttons, cards, modals, inputs, dropdowns, tooltips, or any other visual primitive, even as a "small wrapper" or "just this once".
- **NO hand-styled HTML elements as UI.** Do not use raw `<button>`, `<input>`, `<select>`, `<textarea>`, `<dialog>`, etc. styled with Tailwind classes in place of a shadcn component.
- **NO alternate component libraries** (MUI, Chakra, Ant Design, Mantine, Radix Themes, Headless UI, daisyUI, etc.). Use of Radix primitives is allowed only indirectly through shadcn components.
- **NO duplicating or re-implementing** a shadcn component under a different name.
- If shadcn does not have a component for a need, **compose existing shadcn components together** (e.g. `Card` + `Button` + `Badge`). Layout-only wrappers (`div`, `section`, `main`) using Tailwind utilities for spacing/flex/grid are fine; they must not introduce their own visual styling for interactive or content elements.
- Do not edit the generated files in `src/components/ui` to invent new visuals. Use component `variant`/`size` props and `className` via `cn` for minor layout adjustments only.

## Setup

shadcn is configured in [components.json](mdc:components.json). UI components live under `@/components/ui` (see [src/components/ui](mdc:src/components/ui)).

If shadcn is **not** initialized (no `components.json`), run:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest init
```

## Adding components

Before building any UI, check whether the component already exists under `src/components/ui/`. If it is missing, install it with the CLI (component name is kebab-case) — never hand-write a substitute:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add button
```

Replace `button` with the needed component (e.g. `card`, `input`, `dialog`).

## Usage

- Import from `@/components/ui/<component>` (e.g. `@/components/ui/button`).
- Prefer shadcn variants and composition patterns over any custom markup.
- Use [src/lib/utils.ts](mdc:src/lib/utils.ts) (`cn`) for class merging when extending shadcn components.

## Theme

- **Base color:** Neutral (`tailwind.baseColor`: `neutral` in `components.json`).
- CSS variables live in [src/app/globals.css](mdc:src/app/globals.css).
- Use semantic utilities (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-primary`, `border-border`, `text-muted-foreground`) instead of raw palette classes (`zinc-*`, `gray-*`, etc.).

## Clerk authentication UI

Clerk sign in and sign up **must** be launched in a **modal**, triggered by **shadcn `Button`** components.

- Every sign in and sign up trigger **must** be a shadcn `Button` (`@/components/ui/button`) wrapped by Clerk's `SignInButton` / `SignUpButton`.
- Always set `mode="modal"` on `SignInButton` and `SignUpButton`. Never use redirect mode (the default) and never link users to a separate sign in / sign up page as the primary flow.
- Pass the shadcn `Button` as the child of the Clerk component. Do **not** let Clerk render its own default unstyled button, and do not use a raw `<button>` or `<a>`.
- Use shadcn variants to distinguish the actions (e.g. `variant="ghost"` or `"outline"` for sign in, default `variant` for sign up).

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD: shadcn Button inside Clerk button, launched as a modal
import { SignInButton, SignUpButton } from "@clerk/nextjs";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";

<SignInButton mode="modal">
  <Button variant="outline">Sign in</Button>
</SignInButton>
<SignUpButton mode="modal">
  <Button>Sign up</Button>
</SignUpButton>

// ❌ BAD: redirect mode (no modal)
<SignInButton>
  <Button>Sign in</Button>
</SignInButton>

// ❌ BAD: custom/raw button instead of a shadcn Button
<SignUpButton mode="modal">
  <button className="rounded bg-blue-600 px-4 py-2 text-white">Sign up</button>
</SignUpButton>

// ❌ BAD: Clerk's default button with no shadcn Button
<SignInButton mode="modal" />
```
